{"term":"dew","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:6398aab44c338a49a0","definition":"Any moisture from the atmosphere condensed by cool bodies upon their surfaces.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["dew-beater","dewberry","dewcap","dewclaw","dewclawed","dew computing","dew-drink","dewdrop","dew-eyed","dewfall","dew-fall","dewless","dewlike","dew point","dew poison","dewret","dewretting","dewshine","dew water","dewworm","honeydew","mountain dew","peppadew","sundew"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dew#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5a180d01def22145dd","definition":"Moisture in the air that settles on plants, etc in the morning or evening, resulting in drops.","example":"And Gideon said vnto God, If thou wilt saue Israel by mine hand, as thou hast said,\nBeholde, I will put a fleece of wooll in the floore: and if the deaw be on the fleece onely, and it bee drie vpon all the earth beside, then shall I know that thou wilt saue Israel by my hande, as thou hast said.\nAnd it was so: for he rose vp early on the morrow, and thrust the fleece together, and wringed the deaw out of the fleece, a bowle full of water.\nAnd Gideon said vnto God, Let not thine anger be hote against me, and I will speake but this once: Let mee prooue, I pray thee, but this once with the fleece. Let it now be drie onely vpon the fleece, and vpon all the ground let there be deaw.\nAnd God did so that night: for it was drie vpon the fleece onely, and there was deaw on all the ground.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["rore"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["dew-beater","dewberry","dewcap","dewclaw","dewclawed","dew computing","dew-drink","dewdrop","dew-eyed","dewfall","dew-fall","dewless","dewlike","dew point","dew poison","dewret","dewretting","dewshine","dew wate